# Human gate on the paths machines can't fully judge: the cross-repo
# contract surface (docs/hosted-platform.md#cross-repo-compatibility item 6).
# CI (ci.yml) catches an accidental break in the *shape* of these files; it
# cannot catch a deliberate-but-wrong change to what the contract itself
# should be. Owner review is the other half.
#
# Last-match-wins, so more specific rules are listed after the general ones
# they refine (none needed here — every rule below is already a leaf).

# Exports maps: what a consumer (editor, cloud, template, any outside
# dependent) is even allowed to import.
packages/*/package.json  @mataleogml

# The REST route contract and the auth vocabulary a hosted `authorize()`
# (docs/hosted-platform.md Part I) will depend on.
packages/core/src/api/routes.ts     @mataleogml
packages/core/src/auth-adapter.ts   @mataleogml

# The preview-bridge protocol (__typren postMessage shape) and the token
# contract marketplace blocks are only allowed to consume (Part II, "Slices
# editor, marketplace, and the token contract").
packages/core/src/ui/preview-bridge.vanilla.ts  @mataleogml
packages/core/src/theme.css                     @mataleogml

# CI itself, and who may change whose approval CI requires.
.github/workflows/  @mataleogml
.github/CODEOWNERS  @mataleogml
